# FUNDA360 DEVOPS & INFRASTRUCTURE ARCHITECTURE GUIDE (DIAG)

## 1. Executive Summary
This guide defines the DevOps and infrastructure architecture for Funda360, an enterprise SaaS school management platform. It ensures high availability, scalability, security, and operational excellence across environments. The architecture supports continuous delivery, observability, disaster recovery, and compliance with POPIA and international standards.

---

## 2. Infrastructure Principles
- **Infrastructure as Code (IaC):** Declarative, version-controlled infrastructure.
- **Immutable Infrastructure:** Deploy new instances instead of patching.
- **GitOps:** Git as the single source of truth for deployments.
- **Automation First:** Automated builds, tests, deployments, monitoring.
- **Security by Design:** Encryption, RBAC, zero trust.
- **Zero Trust:** Continuous identity verification.
- **High Availability:** Multi-zone deployments.
- **Self-Healing:** Auto-restart and failover.
- **Observability:** Logging, metrics, tracing.
- **Scalability:** Horizontal scaling, auto-scaling policies.
- **Cost Optimisation:** Resource monitoring and right-sizing.
- **Resilience:** Disaster recovery and redundancy.

---

## 3. Environment Strategy
| Environment | Purpose | Access Rules | Deployment Rules | Data Management |
|-------------|---------|--------------|------------------|-----------------|
| Local Dev | Developer coding | Developer only | Manual | Synthetic data |
| Sandbox | Feature testing | Developer only | On-demand | Synthetic data |
| QA | Automated testing | QA team | CI/CD | Seed data |
| UAT | Business validation | Product owners | Approved builds | Anonymized data |
| Staging | Pre-production | Restricted | CI/CD | Production-like data |
| Pre-Prod | Final validation | Restricted | Manual approval | Production-like data |
| Production | Live system | Role-based | CI/CD | Real data |
| Training | Onboarding | Trainers | Manual | Synthetic data |
| Disaster Recovery | Failover | Restricted | Automated | Replicated data |

